This is where GitHub has a much better mechanism than asking people to paste fork URLs.

We can create a Naya Intelligent Hub GitHub App.

GitHub Apps are specifically designed for this sort of controlled integration. When a user installs an app, they choose which repositories the application can access, and the app's permissions determine exactly what it can do.

So the UX can literally be:

Connect GitHub

→ GitHub authorization

→ choose the Superbrain repository

→ Connected

And that's it.

No:

"Copy your fork URL."

No:

"Give Naya your GitHub password."

No:

"Paste a personal access token."

Much better.

