🔥 My architectural decision

I would lock these principles:

Principle	Decision
Application runtime	Cloudflare
Canonical engineering source	GitHub
Deployment	Cloudflare Workers Builds / Wrangler
GitHub Actions	Remain paused
Individual Superbrain	Sovereign/private
Fork	Optional way to obtain/install a Superbrain
Hub ↔ GitHub	GitHub App, not pasted tokens/fork URLs
Collective synchronization	Intelligence events, not repositories
Shared object	Extracted/generalized wisdom
Identity	Not part of collective intelligence objects
Participation	Explicit opt-in
Contribution scope	User controlled
Collective feedback	Wisdom flows back to participants
Core protocol	Wisdom Contribution / Collective Intelligence protocol

And I would make one principle almost sacred:

The Collective never needs your life to become intelligent. It only needs the wisdom you deliberately choose to contribute.

That's a very compelling foundation for the Intelligent Hub.

And it solves the fork question cleanly: forking creates/owns a Superbrain; the GitHub App connects that Superbrain to the Hub; the Wisdom Contribution Protocol connects selected intelligence to the Collective.
